 "decision": {
  "draftingJob": {
   "outcome": "changes",
   "changes": [
    "Draft a check only through a surface the issue or the approved spec names: a command, route, page, module or message text it states. Where the issue leaves the interface open (a message's exact wording, a data shape, an element's accessible name, when a retry runs, which of two remedies it allows), the requirement goes to the early question instead of a check that guesses. In the spike, 20 of 42 drafted checks failed on the base on their named assertion and then failed on the merged fix too; read by hand, 17 of those 20 assert something the issue doesn't state (a value, an endpoint, a tool's name, how a script finds its repo, a fixture's label), and 3 assert something it does state yet still fail the fix: one matches a label exactly where the issue shows it beside a count, one reads ambiguous wording the other way from the fix, and one uses a storage key the issue named but the base's own code had already named differently, which the fix followed (checks:all).",
    "Build the stand-in for a base with nothing to start, and the early question, as week 5's main path rather than an edge case: 55 of 108 requirements for new or fixed behavior got no check, because the code the check would enter isn't on the base yet; the drafted definition of this repo's #48 has no check at all (checks:6c5bdbe295e96bc0004a5070788a8b5380fbe98568b4c7eb1f64b3856409171d).",
    "Run the drafting job's own base run the way the gate will: in a fresh temporary checkout of the base, through the repo's own test entry and build. Eight checks in three issues ran only because of build output the job had left in its checkout; on a fresh checkout of the merged fix they ran no test until the spike's harness ran the repo's own build on both sides.",
    "Count checks for behavior that must not change apart from new-behavior checks in the readings: all 12 checks dropped for passing on the base were such guards, which behaved as the design asks (checks:all).",
    "Keep each requirement's criterion whole: the requirement's own text is what its check is written from, so it quotes the criterion in full and its checks name each condition. Two raters agree that the drafted requirements state only 65 of 108 criteria in full (coverage:all); in 23 more, a requirement quotes or paraphrases the criterion but its text drops a condition the criterion states, such as 'only the final reply is sent'."
   ],
   "text": "Week 5's drafting job changes. Its requirements state only 65 of 108 criteria in full (coverage:all), and only 7 of 42 drafted checks fail on the base on a named assertion and pass on the merged fix (checks:all): most new-behavior checks either guess an interface the issue leaves open and fail the merged fix, or are never written because the base has nothing to enter. Week 5 builds the drafting job with the five changes listed here.",
   "cites": [
    "coverage:all",
    "checks:all",
    "checks:6c5bdbe295e96bc0004a5070788a8b5380fbe98568b4c7eb1f64b3856409171d"
   ]
  },
  "goalSteps": {
   "build": false,
   "text": "Week 5 doesn't build goal steps (#581); #581 stays parked until a later reading shows they help. Offered goal steps, the drafting job used them in 1 of the 5 UI issues; there its goal-step journeys proved 0 of 4 against 1 of 5 for its locator journeys (journeys:d33c1873c441c0d29d698c68d4fe511d2ad695f7bbf050ac4fc483cc361a0634:goal-steps, journeys:d33c1873c441c0d29d698c68d4fe511d2ad695f7bbf050ac4fc483cc361a0634:plain). The pooled share is higher with goal steps offered (journeys:all:goal-steps, 6 of 13, against journeys:all:plain, 2 of 13), but all of that rise is one issue whose goal-steps draft used no goal step (journeys:9d99281d7a926796428195061e5b17826676e41785f2d0b4019fcdcbd5a9618d:goal-steps, 6 of 8, against 1 of 7 without), so it measures the variance between two drafts of the same issue, not goal steps. The acting harness itself worked: it gave up on the base where the control didn't exist and acted on the fix.",
   "cites": [
    "journeys:all:goal-steps",
    "journeys:all:plain",
    "journeys:d33c1873c441c0d29d698c68d4fe511d2ad695f7bbf050ac4fc483cc361a0634:goal-steps",
